1
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:23,380
Morning at the counter, steam is on the glass

2
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:28,600
How many cups tomorrow? Look at what has passed

3
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:32,940
Naive says tomorrow is the same as today

4
00:00:32,990 --> 00:00:38,000
So it copies every swing, but one day late

5
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:42,980
Take the last three days and average them out

6
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:47,960
The bumps get smaller and the line calms down

7
00:00:48,010 --> 00:00:52,620
But Thursday rushes in and the line stays low

8
00:00:52,670 --> 00:01:00,420
It only knows the three days that you already know

9
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:19,290
[Instrumental · worked example on screen]

10
00:01:19,890 --> 00:01:24,400
Chasing the dots, chasing the dots

11
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:29,840
Every forecast is wrong, so measure how wrong

12
00:01:29,890 --> 00:01:34,200
Add up the misses, divide by the days

13
00:01:34,250 --> 00:01:39,480
That's your average miss in cups, the MAD

14
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:44,060
Turn it into percent and you can compare

15
00:01:44,110 --> 00:01:49,860
The lowest score wins, the dots don't care

16
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:56,160
Smoothing keeps a running guess from day to day

17
00:01:56,210 --> 00:02:01,320
Old forecast plus a share of the miss, that's the way

18
00:02:01,370 --> 00:02:05,860
Alpha is the dial for how fast you forget

19
00:02:05,910 --> 00:02:10,760
Turn it up, you twitch at every little step

20
00:02:10,810 --> 00:02:15,520
Turn it down, you're steady but you're slow to see

21
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:20,740
Point three sits in the middle, where we want to be

22
00:02:20,790 --> 00:02:25,500
A little closer every round, but Thursday's still too low

23
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:31,460
The pattern's in the week, and the smoothing doesn't know

24
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:52,350
[Instrumental · worked example on screen]

25
00:02:52,950 --> 00:02:57,360
Chasing the dots, chasing the dots

26
00:02:57,410 --> 00:03:02,960
Every forecast is wrong, so measure how wrong

27
00:03:03,010 --> 00:03:07,140
Add up the misses, divide by the days

28
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:12,340
That's your average miss in cups, the MAD

29
00:03:12,390 --> 00:03:17,260
Turn it into percent and you can compare

30
00:03:17,310 --> 00:03:23,340
The lowest score wins, the dots don't care

31
00:03:23,390 --> 00:03:28,320
Line up the weeks and colour every day

32
00:03:28,370 --> 00:03:32,880
Thursday's always high and Friday walks away

33
00:03:32,930 --> 00:03:37,840
Thursday over average gives the index you need

34
00:03:37,890 --> 00:03:42,460
Times last week's level, and the dots agree

35
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:47,320
But every miss is low, and low again

36
00:03:47,370 --> 00:03:52,920
Every week the café climbs by four, my friend

37
00:03:52,970 --> 00:04:00,260
Add the climb, then multiply, and you're nearly there

38
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:21,190
[Instrumental · worked example on screen]

39
00:04:21,790 --> 00:04:25,360
Chasing the dots, now we've caught the beat

40
00:04:25,410 --> 00:04:30,720
Blind to the weekday, you miss by seven to eleven

41
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:36,020
See the season, add the climb, you miss by one

42
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:40,440
Find the pattern first, and the forecast's done

43
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:46,060
Every forecast is wrong, so measure how wrong

44
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:51,280
The lowest score wins, the dots don't care

45
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:56,400
How many cups tomorrow?

46
00:04:56,450 --> 00:05:01,480
Look at what has passed
